Ec2 Instance startup

- A server needs four things to be on a network, and AWS quietly set up all four for you: (the first 3 are handled by where handled automatically by DHCP. The firewall was handled outside in a security
 group)
1. an IP address
2. a route out (a "gateway" that carries traffic beyond your local network)
3. DNS (turning names like google.com into addresses)
4. a firewall

